 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Ya'qub: no plate. A seal for «موثقا من الله», geometric for «الله على ما نقول وكيل» and «إن الحكم إلا لله…», a door for «وادخلوا من أبواب متفرقة» (nothing on the negated «لا تدخلوا من باب واحد»). 68:1-20 is not glossed: «ما كان يغني… إلا حاجة في نفس يعقوب» is too long for one chip and must not be split. No plate in 68 (Ya'qub's knowledge). STAGING v4: c1-c2 at Ya'qub's tents in the desert (12:100). Ya'qub is only a blue drop labelled Ya'qub. Binyamin is a single plain man: in c1 he stands beside his father (66: I will not send him with you), in c2 he stands with his brothers (As-Sa'di 67: when he had sent him with them he advised them). The brothers are a plain group of three in dark robes. c1 (66): Ya'qub speaks (66:1, 66:12); a seal plate for the pledge by Allah (66:7-9); the brothers give their pledge by speaking (66:17); Ya'qub answers (66:19) with a geometric plate for Allah as witness (66:20). c2 (67): Ya'qub's advice (67:1, 67:9, 67:13, 67:23); nothing on the negated one gate (67:3-7), a door plate for entering by separate gates (67:8-11, before the Name), a geometric plate for the judgement is Allah's alone (67:19). Nobody raises hands, nothing glows on Ya'qub. c3 (68) in the town of Egypt: two plain groups of three in dark robes come in from opposite sides (68:2, they entered as their father had told them: by separate gates); Ya'qub is not in Egypt, so no drop, no close-up (his name at 68:19), no plate (his knowledge, 68:21-25), only wide shots and gentle pans."
